  "notes": "Two parameters carry this entry and both come straight off the research row. First, harmony: \"two-chord beds\" is `maxChords` 2 with every family a pair, which is the smallest chord palette in this batch that still uses real progressions rather than a static tonic. Second, the 808: \"heavily glided, follows the vocal's melodic leaps\" is the batch's highest `bass808.slideProb` combined with a `bassline.followRootsProb` of 0.7 — the lowest here apart from Real Boston Richey — because an 808 that chases a vocal is not an 808 that sits on roots. The vocal's own parameters are the high register, the abrupt octave jumps (`octaveJumpProb` 0.42) and the high ornament density the research names. ⚠ `medium` per the research's own rating: artist-level production detail is thin, so the drum layer is deliberately the modern-ATL default the research calls it — syncopated 16th kicks and dense triplet-weighted rolls — rather than an invented signature. ⚠ The occasional major-mode cuts are carried by a low-weight `major` in `scales` rather than by major-key chord families, because the research names the mode and not the progressions. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
